Hi Manuel,

This would be a cool development. But it would take a lot of work. In theory, any model that can be implemented in Stan can also be implemented in brms or other Stan-wrapping packages. There is a nice repo here https://github.com/stan-dev/example-models/tree/master/BPA that has Stan code for several of the hierarchical models you are referring to. The hard part would be creating a class of brms functions that convert a wide variety of occupancy or n-mixture models from standard R syntax to Stan syntax. Same goes for data structures.  It would be great if the brms functions handled model statements and data structures consistent with unmarked functions. Whoever created such functions would provide a huge contribution to the quantitative ecology community.

Best,
Tim

