Dear Anne-Merel,
Just in case you wanted to stick with the individual ch version of the CJS model you can form a posterior P-value using the squared, integrated difference between the empirical cumulative survival curve and the predicted one based on the CJS model. I did something similar for a nest survival analysis (https://academic.oup.com/auk/article/127/2/379/5148495). It's not quite the same as a CJS model, but close enough. I don't think I have the winbugs code anymore, but Josh Schmidt, the lead author might.
Best wishes,
Devin

