I'm struggling to figure out how to stitch together a data simulation for  a multi-state (Chap.9 BPA) and Jolly-Seber (Chap.10 BPA). Specifically, how to deal with individuals entering into the data simulation. Can all individuals enter at time= 0 (i.e. creating a dummy first encounter period, like in the analysis step), and then let the entry probability sort out when each individual is first encountered, or should I try to specify the time of first encounter for individuals as is given in the examples of Jolly-Seber models?

